{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 and Mathlib proof of a lower-bound construction for the Gallai–van der Waerden numbers GW(r; 3, l) of Mao, Ozeki, Robertson and Wang: the least m such that for every n ≥ m, every exact r-colouring of {1, …, n} contains a rainbow 3-term or a monochromatic l-term arithmetic progression. Theorem 1: let l ≥ 4 and let p > l be a prime with p ≡ 1 (mod 8) such that no l consecutive integers in [1, p − 1] have the same Legendre symbol modulo p; let s ≥ 2 and let z colour {0, …, l − 1} onto s colours with no rainbow 3-term progression. Colour x in [1, (l − 1)p + 1] by its quadratic character of x − 1 (two colours) when x ≢ 1 (mod p), and the point x = 1 + kp by the new colour 2 + z(k). This colouring uses all s + 2 colours and has no rainbow 3-term and no monochromatic l-term progression, so GW(s + 2; 3, l) > (l − 1)p + 1. The formalization proves Theorem 1 for every such l, p, s and z, the resulting bound for GW (unconditionally for every threshold with the defining property, and for the number itself given that a threshold exists), and the instance (l, p) = (4, 17), which gives GW(4; 3, 4) > 52 and GW(5; 3, 4) > 52.",
